// test_aa_integ_s5.cpp
//
// aa-integ-s5: see SPECIFICATION.md. AA p.11 (the audio location, length, period, volume and data registers, the audio bits
// of ADKCON) and p.27 (SERDAT, SERDATR): P1 to P20, graded on fx68k and TG68K alike. Every run selects the AA chip set with
// chipset_config = $10 (cpu_config = 0).
//
// prog_run.s executes the script that the test places in Chip memory (SPECIFICATION.md section 7); the headers s5_*.h hold the
// script builder, the capture, the shared anchors (fixture, G-S0, G-C) and one function per proposition.
//
// NMH_MUTATE=<selector> runs one contrast: only the proposition the selector names runs (the shared selectors FIXTURE, G0, GC,
// GD, GF, GT, GBRK and GRXD run every proposition they apply to), with the one stimulus the record describes, through the same
// comparators; a record's label prints FAIL (red) or, for a live input through a comparator that is red without it, PASS
// (green). Where a proposition runs the four channels in turn, a run with a selector covers channel 0. NMH_ONLY=P2,P5 restricts
// a run to the named propositions. `make test` leaves both unset and runs no mutant.
//
// MUTATION P1-FIXTURE stimulus red NMH_MUTATE=FIXTURE: every run loads prog_run_nofix.bin, which stores no $BEEF constant; TG68K FAIL, fx68k FAIL. Also printing FAIL on both (19 line(s), by suffix of the label and proposition): -FIXTURE (P2-P20). NOT GRADED on both (68 line(s)): the aggregate line (P1-P20); -A (P1, P2, P16); -B (P1, P2, P16); -C (P1, P2, P16); -BYTES (P3); -ORDER (P3); -SAME (P3); -LEN-2 (P4); -LEN-3 (P4); -LEVEL-2 (P4); -LEVEL-3 (P4); -TWO-2 (P4); -TWO-3 (P4); -LEVELS (P5, P9-P11); -PAIR (P5); -LIN (P6); -SIGN (P6); -ZERO (P6, P17); -ADK (P9-P15); -RUNS (P12-P15); -D (P16); -E (P16); -ONE (P17); -REPEAT (P18); -STOP (P18); -W (P18); -BACK (P19); -DATA (P19); -RBF (P20); -TBE (P20).
// MUTATION P1-G-S0 stimulus red NMH_MUTATE=G0: before the baseline INTENA = $8080 and ADKCON = $8001 are written and the baseline leaves out its INTENA and ADKCON writes; TG68K FAIL, fx68k FAIL. Also printing FAIL on both (20 line(s), by suffix of the label and proposition): -G-S0 (P2-P20); -PRE-CLEAR (P17). NOT GRADED on both (68 line(s)): the aggregate line (P1-P20); -A (P1, P2, P16); -B (P1, P2, P16); -C (P1, P2, P16); -BYTES (P3); -ORDER (P3); -SAME (P3); -LEN-2 (P4); -LEN-3 (P4); -LEVEL-2 (P4); -LEVEL-3 (P4); -TWO-2 (P4); -TWO-3 (P4); -LEVELS (P5, P9-P11); -PAIR (P5); -LIN (P6); -SIGN (P6); -ZERO (P6, P17); -ADK (P9-P15); -RUNS (P12-P15); -D (P16); -E (P16); -ONE (P17); -REPEAT (P18); -STOP (P18); -W (P18); -BACK (P19); -DATA (P19); -RBF (P20); -TBE (P20). The first S0 write of INTENA and ADKCON is missing, so a precondition that reads INTENAR after it goes with G-S0.
// MUTATION P1-G-C stimulus red NMH_MUTATE=GC: the poll of the colour-clock anchor reads VPOSR (offset 004) in place of VHPOSR; TG68K FAIL, fx68k FAIL. Also printing FAIL on both (19 line(s), by suffix of the label and proposition): -G-C (P2-P20). NOT GRADED on both (68 line(s)): the aggregate line (P1-P20); -A (P1, P2, P16); -B (P1, P2, P16); -C (P1, P2, P16); -BYTES (P3); -ORDER (P3); -SAME (P3); -LEN-2 (P4); -LEN-3 (P4); -LEVEL-2 (P4); -LEVEL-3 (P4); -TWO-2 (P4); -TWO-3 (P4); -LEVELS (P5, P9-P11); -PAIR (P5); -LIN (P6); -SIGN (P6); -ZERO (P6, P17); -ADK (P9-P15); -RUNS (P12-P15); -D (P16); -E (P16); -ONE (P17); -REPEAT (P18); -STOP (P18); -W (P18); -BACK (P19); -DATA (P19); -RBF (P20); -TBE (P20).
// MUTATION P1-G-D stimulus red NMH_MUTATE=GD: the DMACON write that starts the channels is $8000 | mask (DMAEN left out); TG68K FAIL, fx68k FAIL. Also printing FAIL on both (41 line(s), by suffix of the label and proposition): -G-F (P1-P4, P6-P8, P15); -PRE-ANCHOR (P1); -G-D (P2-P4, P6-P15); -G-W (P2, P3); -G-P (P3, P12-P14); -PRE-SCALE (P3, P6, P7); -G-P-2 (P4); -G-P-3 (P4); -G-W-2 (P4); -G-W-3 (P4); -PRE-CAL-2 (P4); -PRE-CAL-3 (P4); -PRE-BLOCKS (P8); -PRE-CAL (P9-P11). NOT GRADED on both (46 line(s)): the aggregate line (P1-P4, P6-P15); -A (P1, P2); -B (P1, P2); -C (P1, P2); -BYTES (P3); -ORDER (P3); -SAME (P3); -LEN-2 (P4); -LEN-3 (P4); -LEVEL-2 (P4); -LEVEL-3 (P4); -TWO-2 (P4); -TWO-3 (P4); -LIN (P6); -SIGN (P6); -ZERO (P6); -ADK (P9-P15); -LEVELS (P9-P11); -RUNS (P12-P15). The selector stops every fetch, so every line that needs a fetch of the proposition it runs goes with it.
